# Gitignored files COPIED (not symlinked) into each Orca worktree, so every
# worktree owns a private copy it can edit without touching the primary.
# See orca.yaml for the symlinked (shared) dependency dirs.

# App config. Copied — NOT shared — precisely so each worktree can point at its
# own database/queue and avoid the collisions below. After a worktree is
# created, edit its .env:
#   DB_DATABASE=seatplus_<worktree>   # give each worktree its own pgsql DB
#                                     # (createdb it first) so parallel
#                                     # migrate:fresh runs don't wipe each other
#   REDIS_PREFIX=<worktree>:          # isolate cache keys on the shared Redis
#   REDIS_DB / REDIS_QUEUE            # separate Horizon queues if running >1
.env

# composer-merge path-repo overrides pointing at /packages (generated by
# `composer run local:on`). Copied so a worktree keeps resolving seatplus/*
# locally; regenerate with `composer run local:on` if package paths drift.
composer.local.json

# ── NOT solved by this file — read before running suites in parallel ──────────
# phpunit.xml pins DB_DATABASE=laravel with force="true" in EVERY package, so
# test runs ignore the per-worktree .env above and ALL hit the single `laravel`
# Postgres DB. Two worktrees running `composer run test` at once will corrupt
# each other's migrations. Until phpunit's forced DB name is made per-worktree,
# run test suites SERIALLY across worktrees (app/dev usage in parallel is fine).
# Browser tests are unaffected here — they only run in the "Browser (vs core)"
# CI job, not locally.
